Z||000000||fropuff||03-28-2001||12:23 AM||||Hey there.  I'm wondering if anyone knows about the turbo setup that Dennis LaGrua did on a 2.8 Fiero.  The website he has now is a turbo for the 3.4L on his 87 GT.  I was wondering if there's a different site for this one; it's the one I'm looking for.  Is it the same setup...a Ford Thunderbird turbo?  Thanks a lot!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||6
Z||000001||zeusrekning||03-28-2001||03:08 AM||||Yes that was the same setup he had on the 2.8<BR>He just added a 3.4 later||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||03-28-2001||08:47 AM||||Okay.  Thanks.  That's what I would do if my 2.8 ever went.  Just drop in a 3.1/3.4.  This setup looks a little complicated for a dumbass like me.  Does anyone know of anywhere that sells a turbo kit for ~$1500?  I know Stroker said he was going to start a kit, but no one knows were he is.  Thanks a lot.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Predator||03-28-2001||11:57 AM||||The only complete Turbo Kit I know of for the Fiero is the Design One Systems kit, and it runs $3,000. <A HREF="http://www.design1systems.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.design1systems.com</A> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||03-29-2001||05:23 PM||||I was hoping that I could find another source for cheaper turbo kits, but that's a no go.  I was hoping I could contact Stroker to ask him, but no one has said where he is.  Is he still around?  I was also wondering if there were any turbo experts here in the Midwest (MN, IA, ND, SD, WI, or even the Canadian border of MN)  I am wondering because I really need someone that would be willing to build me up an turbo kit like Dennis' on my 2.8.  I would buy all the parts needed; that person would make a good amount, depending on the work required.  They could also drive it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Please help!  Thanks a lot guys.  Talk to you later!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fropuff||03-30-2001||12:28 AM||||I just talked to one guy, and he has a kit from a company called IFG, a California company.  Anyway, it's a twin turbo kit, but it's not available any more.  Too bad.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jay||03-30-2001||05:55 PM||||Try Race-Tech, in Toronto.  They've got an 85GT with a turbo and intercooler on it that blows away my Northstar.  At least it did last summer, we'll have to see about this year.  Anyway, they specialize in Fiero's.  416-747-5728 ask for Joe or Mirriame.  You'll save a bundle on the exchange!  web site is <A HREF="http://www.racetechauto.com" TARGET=_blank>www.racetechauto.com</A> <BR>e-mail is racetek@idirect.com||||reg||10
